/T (3.5\) truncates toward zero \(-3\), math.floor\(-3.5\) goes toward minus infinity \(-4\), and round\(- 3.5\) gives -4 because the tie goes to the even integer. For a below-standard reading such as fat = 3.1, the raw step count is -3.999999999999999, so int\(\) returns -3 and under-penalises the farmer by one step.)
/E (3.5\) truncates toward zero \(-3\), math.floor\(-3.5\) goes toward minus infinity \(-4\), and round\(- 3.5\) gives -4 because the tie goes to the even integer. For a below-standard reading such as fat = 3.1, the raw step count is -3.999999999999999, so int\(\) returns -3 and under-penalises the farmer by one step.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [73]
