1209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 229 0 R
/T (Both are O\(L\) time and O\(1\) space for an input of L characters \(L is tiny and bounded\). The try/except version is shorter, and on valid input it is faster; on invalid input the exception makes it slower. The string-method version is longer but stricter: it accepts only the formats the clerk is meant to type, whereas float\(\) also accepts exponents \(and, in Python, underscores such as 1_0\). Neither is wrong; try/except plus range and `isfinite` checks is the simpler choice, and a strict pattern check should be added if the co-operative wants to forbid exponent forms.)
/E (Both are O\(L\) time and O\(1\) space for an input of L characters \(L is tiny and bounded\). The try/except version is shorter, and on valid input it is faster; on invalid input the exception makes it slower. The string-method version is longer but stricter: it accepts only the formats the clerk is meant to type, whereas float\(\) also accepts exponents \(and, in Python, underscores such as 1_0\). Neither is wrong; try/except plus range and `isfinite` checks is the simpler choice, and a strict pattern check should be added if the co-operative wants to forbid exponent forms.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
