2811 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 257 0 R
/T (The volunteer's calculator failed for three reasons that this assignment isolated and fixed: money was held as binary floats, step counts were taken with fragile expressions, and the rates were typed in several places. The final design uses exact decimals built from strings, rounds each payment to the paisa under an explicit rule, counts steps with a correctly rounded expression, and keeps every rate in one rate card. It handled 3,000,000 entries - a district-union payment run - in a few seconds with constant memory, and the Task 12 change \(two-decimal readings, seasonal cards, volume bonus\) was absorbed by a small, tested modification.)
/E (The volunteer's calculator failed for three reasons that this assignment isolated and fixed: money was held as binary floats, step counts were taken with fragile expressions, and the rates were typed in several places. The final design uses exact decimals built from strings, rounds each payment to the paisa under an explicit rule, counts steps with a correctly rounded expression, and keeps every rate in one rate card. It handled 3,000,000 entries - a district-union payment run - in a few seconds with constant memory, and the Task 12 change \(two-decimal readings, seasonal cards, volume bonus\) was absorbed by a small, tested modification.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
