4863 0 obj
<<
/Title (Both designs are O\(n\) in time and in space for the data itself, but the first one also makes the program text grow as O\(n\). In the measurement, n = 30,000 needs 120,001 source lines and 90,001 variable names and takes 1523.0 ms to compile and run, against 4 lines and 14.7 ms for the list design. One tuple of three floats occupies 64 bytes plus 24 bytes per float, so the data cost is about the same; the difference is code, not data.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4832 0 R
/Prev 4904 0 R
>>
