5210 0 obj
<<
/Title (An honest result: on both data sets even the plain float sum, after rounding once at the end, gave the exact total. Its error \(about 6e-10 Rs\) is far below half a paisa. So float is not unsuitable because sums drift; it is unsuitable because of equality tests and tie-rounding of single payments, which Task 10 shows affects about 4 % of payments. Decimal costs 104 bytes per value instead of 24, but only a little more time per addition than float.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5190 0 R
>>
endobj
