5258 0 obj
<<
/Title (The automatic suite of 23 tests ran in about 0.17 ms. For manual testing I assumed 20 seconds per case \(type three to five values, read the result, compare it with the expected value\); this figure is an assumption, not a measurement, but even if it is wrong by a factor of ten the difference is enormous: about 7.7 minutes per full re-run by hand against a fraction of a millisecond, and the cost multiplies by the number of changes \(20 changes: about 2.5 hours against a few milliseconds\). Both approaches are O\(T\) in the number of tests T; the constant factor, the risk of a mistyped input and the temptation to skip some cases are what make manual testing impractical after every change.)
/Dest [43 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5235 0 R
/Prev 5285 0 R
>>
endobj
