/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5264 0 R
/Prev 5321 0 R
>>
endobj
5295 0 obj
<<
/Title (The farmer receives a delivery slip for each payment, so the ten-day total must equal the sum of the rounded slips. Rounding each payment first is therefore the rule that reconciles with the slips. I did not have a bank statement to confirm what the bank itself does. The experiments pool all entries into one total, as a centre or block would; one farmer's ten-day total has only about 20 entries, so the difference for a single farmer is much smaller.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5265 0 R
>>
endobj
